{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy is coverage-biased in clear space, uses one-shot directed recovery after obstacle events, reserves backward motion only for front-obstacle escape, and returns to forward exploration immediately when path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted, while safety-critical obstacle events can redirect recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in G, and place the task logic in E.",
    "Use clear->forward as default exploration, left/right obstacles -> directed turn away, front obstacle -> brief backward escape then turn, with full_rotate only as a last-resort front-blocked recovery."
  ],
